          "text": "The dominant reflections index on an orthorhombic cell with approximately:\n\n\\[\na=13.875\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad b=5.784\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad c=4.906\\ \\text{\u00c5}\n\\]\n\nThe extinction pattern and composition are consistent with an ordered, columbite-derived **Pnma** structure, \\(Z=4\\). Representative indexing is: 200 at 12.75\u00b0, 210 at 19.98\u00b0, 201 at 22.18\u00b0, 400 at 25.66\u00b0, 410 at 30.03\u00b0, 020 at 30.91\u00b0, 220 at 33.56\u00b0, 221 at 38.37\u00b0, 600 at 38.92\u00b0, 402 at 45.25\u00b0, 222 at 50.50\u00b0, and 422 at 55.81\u00b0.\n\nThe heavy-atom topology and unit cell are secure. Oxygen and lithium coordinates below are geometry-regularized powder coordinates and should be finalized by Rietveld refinement.\n\n```cif\ndata_LiNbWO6_primary\n_audit_creation_method\n'Powder-indexed, geometry-regularized structural model'\n_chemical_name_common                 'lithium niobium tungsten oxide'\n_chemical_formula_structural          'LiNbWO6'\n_chemical_formula_sum                 'Li4 Nb4 W4 O24'\n_chemical_formula_weight              379.68\n_cell_formula_units_Z                 4\n\n_cell_length_a                        13.8750\n_cell_length_b                         5.7840\n_cell_length_c                         4.9060\n_cell_angle_alpha                     90\n_cell_angle_beta                      90\n_cell_angle_gamma                     90\n_cell_volume                          393.56\n\n_space_group_crystal_system           orthorhombic\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt             'P n m a'\n_space_group_IT_number                62\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn         6.405\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '-x+1/2,-y,z+1/2'\n3  '-x,y+1/2,-z'\n4  'x+1/2,-y+1/2,-z+1/2'\n5  '-x,-y,-z'\n6  'x+1/2,y,-z+1/2'\n7  'x,-y+1/2,z'\n8  '-x+1/2,y+1/2,z+1/2'\n\nloop_\n_atom_type_symbol\n_atom_type_oxidation_number\nLi  1\nNb  5\nW   6\nO  -2\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nLi1  Li  4  c   0.0008  0.2500  0.0040  1.0  1.20\nNb1  Nb  4  c   0.1658  0.2500  0.4935  1.0  0.45\nW1   W   4  c   0.3341  0.2500  0.0075  1.0  0.40\nO1   O   8  d   0.0879  0.0615  0.2675  1.0  0.75\nO2   O   8  d   0.2578  0.0580  0.2205  1.0  0.75\nO3   O   8  d   0.4094  0.0605  0.2215  1.0  0.75\n```\n\nA surviving ordering alternative is obtained by exchanging the Nb1 and W1 site assignments in this CIF. It has identical peak positions but different intensities. Several features\u2014most notably the peak near 34.18\u00b0\u2014do not fall exactly on the indexed Pnma subcell and may indicate a weak ordering superstructure or a secondary polymorph; the CIF above therefore represents the dominant average structure.",
